1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:08,765
High in the Andes, near the shore of Lake Titicaca, a wall of red rock has been cut into the shape of a door.

2
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:10,158
Seven metres tall.

3
00:00:10,158 --> 00:00:11,550
Seven metres wide.

4
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:14,800
And it opens onto nothing but solid stone.

5
00:00:15,266 --> 00:00:17,626
They call it the Gate of the Gods.

6
00:00:17,626 --> 00:00:18,390
Aramu Muru.

7
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:26,233
A portal, people say, that an ancient priest once opened with a golden disk, and walked through, never to return.

8
00:00:26,699 --> 00:00:27,473
A stargate.

9
00:00:27,473 --> 00:00:29,232
An interdimensional door.

10
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:31,412
A relic of a lost civilization.

11
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:33,733
You have probably seen the clips.

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,439
Tonight we try something different.

13
00:00:36,439 --> 00:00:38,550
We do not start at the beginning.

14
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:40,533
We start now, and press rewind.

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:49,182
Decade by decade, century by century, we roll the story backwards, and watch for the exact moment the portal appears.

16
00:00:49,182 --> 00:00:52,400
Then we score the evidence and give a verdict.

17
00:00:56,866 --> 00:00:57,744
Chapter one.

18
00:00:57,744 --> 00:00:59,135
Twenty twenty-five.

19
00:00:59,135 --> 00:01:09,966
A post on X goes viral, and the tabloids follow: a mysterious gate cut into a Peruvian mountain that could reveal a long-lost advanced civilization.

20
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:12,632
Television had already been there.

21
00:01:12,632 --> 00:01:17,676
On Ancient Aliens, one presenter called it a gateway that doesn't go anywhere.

22
00:01:17,676 --> 00:01:25,566
Another suggested the sun disk might have had an extraterrestrial connection, a technological device with which to travel.

23
00:01:26,033 --> 00:01:28,127
Visitors arrive by the busload.

24
00:01:28,127 --> 00:01:36,033
They kneel in the niche, press their foreheads to the stone, and report vibrations, visions, music, tunnels of light.

25
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:49,772
But even the same article that sold the mystery admits the key point: no unusual electromagnetic fields, no radiation, no geological anomaly has ever been measured there.

26
00:01:49,772 --> 00:01:51,099
Just carved rock.

27
00:01:51,566 --> 00:01:55,041
And notice how the facts wobble as they travel.

28
00:01:55,041 --> 00:02:01,842
One Argentine paper, repeating the same post, said the gate was found in nineteen sixty-six.

29
00:02:01,842 --> 00:02:04,208
A typo, for nineteen ninety-six.

30
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:06,500
The dates are already slipping.

31
00:02:06,966 --> 00:02:20,866
What the clips rarely mention: the site sits on the land of an Aymara community, Mulla Contihueco, more than three thousand eight hundred metres up, and it was sacred to them long before it went viral.

32
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:23,812
So the internet says ancient mystery.

33
00:02:23,812 --> 00:02:27,966
Let's rewind, to the year the outside world first heard of it.

34
00:02:28,433 --> 00:02:29,380
Chapter two.

35
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:30,958
Nineteen ninety-six.

36
00:02:30,958 --> 00:02:43,266
A story spreads on the early web: a local mountain guide, José Luis Delgado Mamani, has stumbled on a huge carved door while hiking the hills of Hayu Marca.

37
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:45,410
His words became famous.

38
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:47,856
When I saw it, I almost passed out.

39
00:02:47,856 --> 00:02:56,733
I had dreamed of it for years: a path of pink marble, the small door open, and a brilliant blue light from a shimmering tunnel.

40
00:02:57,199 --> 00:03:00,704
That nineteen ninety-six article goes further.

41
00:03:00,704 --> 00:03:08,476
It says he alerted archaeologists in Puno, La Paz and Lima, and the site was soon besieged by experts.

42
00:03:08,476 --> 00:03:11,599
We could find no report from any of them.

43
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:27,666
Then it adds a local legend: heroes who passed through a gateway to join the gods, and an Inca priest named Aramu Maru, of the temple of the seven rays, carrying a golden disk called the key of the gods of the seven rays.

44
00:03:28,133 --> 00:03:33,196
Even that article admits the professional opinion: there is no actual door.

45
00:03:33,196 --> 00:03:38,866
The frame, the entrance and the back of the niche are all carved from the same rock.

46
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:42,000
Now look closer at the discoverer.

47
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Visitors who knew him call him Jorge Luis Delgado, a tour operator who ran a hotel in nearby Chucuito.

48
00:03:50,466 --> 00:03:54,791
In a nineteen ninety-nine travel article he explained his search.

49
00:03:54,791 --> 00:04:03,108
Years earlier he had read a book called Secret of the Andes, and spent about nineteen years looking for its hidden monastery.

50
00:04:03,108 --> 00:04:04,838
He dreamed of pink stones.

51
00:04:04,838 --> 00:04:07,433
A shaman told him to follow the energy.

52
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,494
And the dates do not hold still either.

53
00:04:10,494 --> 00:04:16,682
He told that writer he had permission to bring pilgrims to the gate from nineteen ninety-two.

54
00:04:16,682 --> 00:04:21,206
Another writer describes his own expeditions there from ninety-five.

55
00:04:21,206 --> 00:04:24,466
Wikipedia just says, the early nineteen nineties.

56
00:04:24,933 --> 00:04:29,348
And for the people who lived there, nothing was discovered at all.

57
00:04:29,348 --> 00:04:34,699
They already had names for it: Willka Uta, and Ajayu Marka, the city of spirits.

58
00:04:35,166 --> 00:04:38,124
So the guide brought the outside world.

59
00:04:38,124 --> 00:04:41,841
But the name Aramu Muru, the monastery, the disk?

60
00:04:41,841 --> 00:04:43,813
Those came from that book.

61
00:04:43,813 --> 00:04:44,800
Rewind again.

62
00:04:45,266 --> 00:04:46,232
Chapter three.

63
00:04:46,232 --> 00:04:47,542
Nineteen sixty-one.

64
00:04:47,542 --> 00:04:52,233
A book appears: Secret of the Andes, by a mysterious Brother Philip.

65
00:04:52,699 --> 00:04:54,799
Brother Philip was a pen name.

66
00:04:54,799 --> 00:05:08,933
The author was George Hunt Williamson, an American flying saucer contactee, one of the witnesses of George Adamski's claimed meeting with a man from Venus in the California desert in nineteen fifty-two.

67
00:05:09,399 --> 00:05:14,529
Williamson took messages from space brothers with a home-made Ouija board.

68
00:05:14,529 --> 00:05:21,600
He was expelled from university in nineteen fifty-one and had no degree, yet he called himself doctor.

69
00:05:22,066 --> 00:05:37,500
His book tells of Lemuria, a sinking continent in the Pacific, and of Lord Aramu Muru, a sage who flew to Lake Titicaca in a silver needle airship, carrying sacred scrolls and the Golden Sun Disc of Mu.

70
00:05:37,966 --> 00:05:47,167
There, the book says, he founded the Monastery of the Brotherhood of the Seven Rays, in a hidden valley on the Peruvian side of the lake.

71
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:51,533
The disc was later lent to the Inca at their Sun Temple in Cusco.

72
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:00,435
Lemuria itself is a nineteenth-century idea, born in Theosophy, with no support from geology or archaeology.

73
00:06:00,435 --> 00:06:10,666
And here is the twist: according to a contactee writer who knew Delgado, the book never even mentions the stone door at Hayu Marca.

74
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:20,702
So the seven rays, the monastery, the golden disc and the name Aramu Muru all trace back to one American contactee's channelled book.

75
00:06:20,702 --> 00:06:22,933
A book about a different place.

76
00:06:23,399 --> 00:06:29,015
Over the following decades, readers went looking for that monastery around the lake.

77
00:06:29,015 --> 00:06:33,962
When a striking carved door turned up, the book's hero was waiting for it.

78
00:06:33,962 --> 00:06:35,366
Name and place fused.

79
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:40,147
But the story we heard says the priest fled the Spanish conquest.

80
00:06:40,147 --> 00:06:43,199
So let's rewind four hundred years, and check.

81
00:06:43,666 --> 00:06:44,638
Chapter four.

82
00:06:44,638 --> 00:06:46,207
The fifteen thirties.

83
00:06:46,207 --> 00:06:48,822
Part of the legend is real history.

84
00:06:48,822 --> 00:06:56,966
In fifteen thirty-three Spanish conquistadors stripped the gold from the Coricancha, the Sun Temple of Cusco.

85
00:06:57,433 --> 00:07:11,333
The popular tale: a priest named Aramu Muru escapes south with a golden sun disk, reaches the door at Hayu Marca, places the disk in a small hollow, and the rock opens in blue light.

86
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:18,332
But the Spanish chroniclers recorded Andean priests, temples and treasures in great detail.

87
00:07:18,332 --> 00:07:21,634
No chronicle names a priest called Aramu Muru.

88
00:07:21,634 --> 00:07:27,233
Even a writer who believes the door is a portal calls that priest story false.

89
00:07:27,699 --> 00:07:29,038
The keyhole is real.

90
00:07:29,038 --> 00:07:32,451
There is a small round depression inside the niche.

91
00:07:32,451 --> 00:07:36,266
Pilgrims press a disk, a hand, or their forehead into it.

92
00:07:36,733 --> 00:07:42,104
Some local healers told one visitor that a green stone, umiña, once sat there.

93
00:07:42,104 --> 00:07:45,133
Others simply say the human body is the key.

94
00:07:45,133 --> 00:07:51,399
These are living beliefs, and they deserve respect, but they are not evidence of a machine.

95
00:07:51,866 --> 00:08:05,866
Archaeologist Charles Stanish, a leading expert on Lake Titicaca, quotes this very legend from a website, and files it where it belongs: in the alternative literature, not in the historical record.

96
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:08,866
So the priest and the disk are modern.

97
00:08:08,866 --> 00:08:13,733
Rewind another century, and look at the rock itself, through Andean eyes.

98
00:08:14,199 --> 00:08:15,181
Chapter five.

99
00:08:15,181 --> 00:08:16,843
The fourteen hundreds.

100
00:08:16,843 --> 00:08:27,266
This shore was the heartland of the Lupaqa, an Aymara-speaking kingdom ruled from Chucuito, absorbed by the Inca in the fifteenth century.

101
00:08:27,733 --> 00:08:31,374
For Andean peoples, the landscape itself was alive.

102
00:08:31,374 --> 00:08:41,299
Mountains, springs, caves and unusual rocks could be huacas, sacred places where the powers of the world were near, and received offerings.

103
00:08:41,766 --> 00:08:45,655
The Inca loved one shape above all: the trapezoid.

104
00:08:45,655 --> 00:08:50,244
Doors, windows and niches lean inward, narrower at the top.

105
00:08:50,244 --> 00:08:53,433
Niches held offerings and sacred objects.

106
00:08:53,899 --> 00:08:55,700
And they built false doors.

107
00:08:55,700 --> 00:09:01,833
At the Temple of the Moon near Machu Picchu, niches and fake doors are cut into living rock.

108
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:05,100
Doors that were never meant to be walked through.

109
00:09:05,566 --> 00:09:08,558
Look at Hayu Marca again with that in mind.

110
00:09:08,558 --> 00:09:10,159
A great smoothed panel.

111
00:09:10,159 --> 00:09:16,700
A smaller niche at its foot, the height of a person, where you stand or kneel facing the rock.

112
00:09:17,166 --> 00:09:24,242
Many researchers read it as an Inca-period altar or monumental shrine that was never finished.

113
00:09:24,242 --> 00:09:26,425
Work began, and then stopped.

114
00:09:26,425 --> 00:09:30,866
Some historians call the rough carving older than the Inca.

115
00:09:31,333 --> 00:09:40,409
A recent report says pottery found on the surface points to long ceremonial reuse by Tiwanaku, the Lupaqa and the Inca.

116
00:09:40,409 --> 00:09:45,366
But no one has ever excavated the site, so there is no firm date.

117
00:09:45,833 --> 00:09:50,613
The Aymara names fit this reading far better than any stargate.

118
00:09:50,613 --> 00:09:51,448
Willka Uta.

119
00:09:51,448 --> 00:09:52,358
Ajayu Marka.

120
00:09:52,358 --> 00:09:59,566
A threshold between the living and the world of the ancestors, still used for ceremonies today.

121
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:03,411
Some say the hands that cut it were older still.

122
00:10:03,411 --> 00:10:05,100
Rewind a thousand years.

123
00:10:05,566 --> 00:10:06,445
Chapter six.

124
00:10:06,445 --> 00:10:08,056
Around AD six hundred.

125
00:10:08,056 --> 00:10:15,600
South of the lake, the city of Tiwanaku became the great power of the region, famous for its stonework.

126
00:10:16,066 --> 00:10:20,712
The comparison everyone makes is the Gate of the Sun at Tiwanaku.

127
00:10:20,712 --> 00:10:25,143
But that is a free-standing gateway covered in carved figures.

128
00:10:25,143 --> 00:10:28,145
Hayu Marca is plain, and cut into a cliff.

129
00:10:28,145 --> 00:10:31,433
They share a word, gate, and very little else.

130
00:10:31,899 --> 00:10:40,679
One Andean writer, studying the tooling, sees the work of the Tiwanaku state, between AD four hundred and eleven hundred.

131
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:42,566
Others see Inca technique.

132
00:10:42,566 --> 00:10:47,500
A popular science article notes the style matches neither perfectly.

133
00:10:47,966 --> 00:10:50,981
What everyone agrees on is the material.

134
00:10:50,981 --> 00:10:54,222
This is sandstone, far softer than granite.

135
00:10:54,222 --> 00:10:58,367
Stone hammers, harder stones and patience can shape it.

136
00:10:58,367 --> 00:10:59,800
No lasers required.

137
00:11:00,266 --> 00:11:01,854
And the alien version?

138
00:11:01,854 --> 00:11:10,441
It needs a builder who left no tools, no workshop, no debris, no record, and carved a door that opens onto solid stone.

139
00:11:10,441 --> 00:11:12,966
There is simply no evidence for it.

140
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:16,801
Inca, Tiwanaku, or older: human, either way.

141
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:20,245
But there is one more layer before the hands.

142
00:11:20,245 --> 00:11:21,700
Rewind all the way.

143
00:11:22,166 --> 00:11:23,209
Chapter seven.

144
00:11:23,209 --> 00:11:23,954
Deep time.

145
00:11:23,954 --> 00:11:28,946
Long before any people, layers of red sediment hardened into stone.

146
00:11:28,946 --> 00:11:35,799
Geological folding tilted them, and erosion carved them into a forest of crests and pillars.

147
00:11:36,266 --> 00:11:42,879
Walk through Hayu Marca and you will see a puma, a condor, a snake, even a sleeping woman.

148
00:11:42,879 --> 00:11:44,495
Guides point them out.

149
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:46,185
Almost all are natural.

150
00:11:46,185 --> 00:11:50,299
Our brains are built to find faces and figures in stone.

151
00:11:50,766 --> 00:11:53,679
That is part of why this hillside felt powerful.

152
00:11:53,679 --> 00:12:00,233
A place where the rock already looked built, and where people chose to finish the work with their own hands.

153
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:03,094
And the sensations people feel?

154
00:12:03,094 --> 00:12:07,497
At this altitude the air holds about a third less oxygen.

155
00:12:07,497 --> 00:12:11,900
Unacclimatised visitors get dizzy, euphoric, suggestible.

156
00:12:12,366 --> 00:12:21,784
Add wind humming across a concave niche, sun-warmed stone at dusk, and the expectation of a portal, and you have a powerful experience.

157
00:12:21,784 --> 00:12:25,133
Real to the person who feels it, but not a door.

158
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:28,642
The real danger at the gate is not aliens.

159
00:12:28,642 --> 00:12:38,133
Candle wax, oils and burnt resin poured on the soft sandstone are damaging the surface, and the site still lacks formal protection.

160
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,303
The tape is fully rewound.

161
00:12:40,303 --> 00:12:44,233
Now we can play it forward and see the whole story in order.

162
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,700
Time to score the Gate of the Gods.

163
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:51,010
Carved by people into natural sandstone: evidence.

164
00:12:51,010 --> 00:12:54,624
A sacred place to Aymara communities: evidence.

165
00:12:54,624 --> 00:12:59,698
Fits the Andean tradition of rock shrines and false doors: likely.

166
00:12:59,698 --> 00:13:02,466
Who carved it, and when: still open.

167
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:11,244
The priest Aramu Muru and the golden disk: a modern myth, from nineteen sixty-one and the nineteen nineties.

168
00:13:11,244 --> 00:13:13,706
A working stargate: no evidence.

169
00:13:13,706 --> 00:13:16,399
Measured energy or anomalies: none.

170
00:13:16,866 --> 00:13:17,769
The verdict.

171
00:13:17,769 --> 00:13:24,689
Hayu Marca is a real, human-carved Andean shrine, probably unfinished, sacred to the Aymara.

172
00:13:24,689 --> 00:13:26,644
The portal is not ancient.

173
00:13:26,644 --> 00:13:34,166
It was born in a nineteen sixty-one contactee book and joined to this rock in the nineteen nineties.

174
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:45,548
Played forward, the story is clear: a sacred rock, a shrine left unfinished, a conquest, a channelled book, a dreaming guide, and finally a viral clip.

175
00:13:45,548 --> 00:13:47,066
Every layer is human.

176
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:51,454
Maybe the real gate here is a gate into how myths are made.

177
00:13:51,454 --> 00:13:58,166
And the people who kept this place sacred long before the cameras deserve the last word in its story.

178
00:13:58,633 --> 00:14:00,628
Which layer surprised you most?

179
00:14:00,628 --> 00:14:06,033
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
